<title>USA: USDA says meat export report notice due this month.</title>
<headline>USDA says meat export report notice due this month.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The White House budget office this week began studying a preliminary USDA proposal to start export sales reports for meat and poultry, USDA Foreign Agriculture Service associate administrator Tim Galvin said Friday.</p>
<p>Galvin said officials from USDA and the White House Office of Management and Budget (OMB) would meet next week to discuss the USDA document.</p>
<p>USDA hopes that OMB will sign off on the document, which calls for public comments on meat export sales reporting, by the end of the month, clearing the way for publication in the Federal Register.</p>
<p>-- Washington Commodities Desk (202) 898-8489</p>
